    activity: "Read Romans 14:1-23 and discuss. Work through invented scenarios of a wedding or festival invitation and decide responses with love and conscience.",
    takeHome: "Read Romans 14 and 15:1-7, 1 Corinthians 8 and 10, and Colossians 2. Write a decision framework. Memorise Romans 14:19.",
    prayer: "Thank God for unity in Christ. Ask for wisdom, tolerance and loyalty to him alone.",
    teacher: "Treat local customs with respect. Avoid dogmatism on disputable matters. Where practices involve spirits or ancestors as objects of worship, teach clearly that worship belongs to God alone while showing compassion for families.",
    assess: "Weekly check: ask learners how to decide about customs and festivals.",
    mcq1: ["What does Romans 14:5 say?", ["Each one should be fully convinced in his own mind", "Everyone must follow my way", "Ignore conscience", "Avoid all days"], 0, "Fully convinced."],
